{"type":"message","message":{"id":"gen-1775346131-ywGm1QUerLhc6BHmvBdh","role":"assistant","created":1775346153,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The issue is that the table format uses multiple years in each row. Let me understand this better. Looking at the structure:\n\n1957 section shows:\n- January 1957: 3.34\n- February 1957: 3.22\n- ...\n- June 1957: 3.58\n\nBut in the same row as June 1957, there's also 1959 and 1961 data.\n\nLet me look more carefully at the structure. Each row has 9 columns:\n1. Month/Period\n2. Treasury bonds (for year 1)\n3. Moody's Aaa (for year 1)\n4. Period (year 2)\n5. Treasury bonds (for year 2)\n6. Moody's Aaa (for year 2)\n7. Period (year 3)\n8. Treasury bonds (for year 3)\n9. Moody's Aaa (for year 3)\n\nSo when I see:\n```\n<td>June</td><td>3.58 2/</td><td>3.91</td><td></td><td>3.88</td><td>4.46</td><td></td><td>4.00</td><td>4.23</td>\n```\n\nThis means:\n- June (month)\n- 1957 Treasury: 3.58\n- 1957 Moody's: 3.91\n- 1959 Treasury: 3.88\n- 1959 Moody's: 4.46\n- 1961 Treasury: 4.00\n- 1961 Moody's: 4.23\n\nI need to build a proper mapping. Let me parse this more carefully.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_860f788734644ec3a23d4b78","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"python3 << 'EOF'\nimport re\n\nwith open('/app/resources/treasury_bulletin_1968_07_page_83.txt', 'r') as f:\n    content = f.read()\n\n# Split into year sections\n# The table header structure shows monthly series\n# Let's build a mapping by tracking year headers\n\njune_yields = {}\n\n# Parse the monthly series section more carefully\n# Years are in the order: 1957, 1959, 1961 in first row block\n# Then 1958, 1960, 1966 in second row block\n# etc.\n\n# Let's identify the columns for each year from the row headers\nmonth_rows = content.split('</tr><tr>')\n\n# Track the years for each column position\n# First, find the year headers\ncurrent_years = [None, None, None]  # For columns 2-3, 4-5, 6-7 (Treasury and Moody's pairs)\n\nfor row in month_rows:\n    # Check for year section headers\n    year_section = re.search(r'<td colspan=\"9\">(\\d{4})</td>', row)\n    if year_section:\n        year = int(year_section.group(1))\n        # Reset the year tracking based on which year block we're in\n        # Looking at the structure: 1957 section has 1957, 1959, 1961 in columns\n        # 1958 section has 1958, 1960, 1966 in columns\n        continue\n    \n    # Look for year indicators in the row (e.g., <td>1963</td> or <td>1959</td>)\n    year_cells = re.findall(r'<td>(\\d{4})</td>', row)\n    \n    # Look for June\n    june_match = re.search(r'<td>June</td>', row)\n    if june_match:\n        # Get all the values in this row\n        values = re.findall(r'<td>([\\d.]+)\\s*(?:2/)?</td>', row)\n        print(f\"June row values: {values}\")\n        print(f\"Year cells in row: {year_cells}\")\n        print(f\"Row: {row[:250]}\")\n        print()\nEOF"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
