{"type":"message","message":{"id":"gen-1775346226-D7baWIqPzjXGunbDtuPU","role":"assistant","created":1775346251,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The issue is that the parsing is accumulating years across different sections. Let me be more careful - I should reset when a new section starts and figure out the exact column-to-year mapping.\n\nLooking at the data more carefully:\n- Section 1957: Years [1957, 1959, 1961], yields [3.58, 3.91, 3.88, 4.46, 4.00, 4.23]\n  - These should map to: 1957→3.58, 1959→3.88, 1961→4.00 (the first value of each pair)\n\n- Section 1958: Years [1958, 1960, 1966, 1962, 1968, 1964], but this seems wrong. Let me re-check.\n\nActually I think I'm accumulating too much. Let me try a different approach - I'll just look at the raw structure and manually map out which column corresponds to which year.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_63cec59c8fe94fb482608c0d","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"python3 << 'EOF'\nimport re\n\nwith open('/app/resources/treasury_bulletin_1968_07_page_83.txt', 'r') as f:\n    content = f.read()\n\n# Let me be more careful - I'll parse each section independently\n# When we hit a new year section header, I'll reset\n\nmonthly_section = content[content.find('Monthly series'):]\nrows = monthly_section.split('</tr><tr>')\n\n# Let me build a proper mapping by understanding the column structure\n# Each month row has this structure:\n# <td>Month</td><td>Yield_Treasury_Year1</td><td>Yield_Moodys_Year1</td>[<td>Year2</td>]<td>Yield_Treasury_Year2</td><td>Yield_Moodys_Year2</td>[<td>Year3</td>]<td>Yield_Treasury_Year3</td><td>Yield_Moodys_Year3</td>\n\n# The years in columns can be identified by looking at:\n# 1. The section header (gives first year)\n# 2. Year markers in the row (give 2nd and 3rd year positions)\n\njune_yields = {}\n\ncurrent_base_year = None\nrow_count = 0\n\nfor row in rows:\n    row_count += 1\n    # Check for year section header\n    header_match = re.search(r'<td colspan=\"9\">(\\d{4})</td>', row)\n    if header_match:\n        current_base_year = int(header_match.group(1))\n        continue\n    \n    # If we're in a June row\n    if '<td>June</td>' in row and current_base_year:\n        # The structure has 3 column pairs of (Treasury, Moody's) each\n        # With year markers potentially in some positions\n        \n        # Get all the cells\n        cells = row.split('</td>')\n        \n        # Let's extract manually based on position\n        # cell[0] = \"June\"\n        # cell[1] = Treasury yield for first year (current_base_year)\n        # cell[2] = Moody's for first year\n        # cell[3] could be empty or year2\n        # cell[4] = Treasury yield for year2\n        # etc.\n        \n        # Find year markers in the row - these tell us which columns have which years\n        # Pattern: <td>YEAR</td>\n        year_markers_pos = []\n        for i, cell in enumerate(cells):\n            yr = re.search(r'(\\d{4})', cell)\n            if yr and int(yr.group(1)) < 2000:\n                year_markers_pos.append((i, int(yr.group(1))))\n        \n        # Extract yields from positions 1, 4, 7 (Treasury yields)\n        # (skipping position 0 which is \"June\", and positions 2,5,7 are Moody's)\n        \n        all_values = re.findall(r'<td>([\\d.]+)\\s*(?:2/)?</td>', row)\n        \n        print(f\"Section starting year: {current_base_year}\")\n        print(f\"Year markers at positions: {year_markers_pos}\")\n        print(f\"All yield values: {all_values}\")\n        \n        # For the first section (1957), values should map to:\n        # 1957: 3.58, 1959: 3.88, 1961: 4.00\n        \n        # Now figure out the mapping based on position of year markers\n        # If no year marker in position 3, then year2 = current_base_year + 2 (i.e., 1959)\n        # If year marker in position 3, that gives us year2\n        \n        # Actually, looking at section 1957:\n        # - No year marker before column pair 2 -> year2 = 1959 (derived from context)\n        # - No year marker before column pair 3 -> year3 = 1961 (derived from context)\n        \n        # This suggests the years are implicitly: \n        # Section year, year+2, year+4 for the three column pairs\n        \n        # Let's verify with section 1958:\n        # Should be: 1958, 1960, 1962 (but we see 1966, 1964, 1968 in the data?)\n        \n        # Wait, there seem to be more years. Let me re-examine the raw content\n        \nprint(\"\\n\\nLet me look at the actual section structure:\")\n# Look at rows that contain year headers after the first few month rows\nfor i, row in enumerate(rows[1:20]):\n    if '<td colspan=\"9\">' in row:\n        year = re.search(r'<td colspan=\"9\">(\\d{4})</td>', row).group(1)\n        print(f\"Section: {year}\")\n    if '<td>196' in row:\n        print(f\"  Row {i}: {row[:200]}\")\nEOF"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
