{"type":"message","message":{"id":"gen-1775346282-dvP5Jz22XWQjf1y07Py6","role":"assistant","created":1775346297,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I can see the issue. The table has a more complex structure where data from different years appears in different row blocks. Looking at the December rows, we see years like 1962, 1968 appearing.\n\nLooking at this more carefully:\n- December row from \"1957\" section has: 3.30 (1957), 4.06 (1962), 4.34 (1968) for Treasury yields\n- December row from \"1958\" section has: 3.80 (1958), 3.87 (1968)\n\nThis is confusing. Let me step back and understand the table format differently. Perhaps each section continues with data from different years.\n\nActually, looking at it again - I think the table is formatted in a specific way:\n- The section headers (like \"1957\") mark where to START reading, but data from multiple years appears in each row block\n- The years shown in the row (like \"1962\", \"1968\") are the actual years for that column\n\nLet me look at the raw table differently. I should look for June in each year from 1957-1968 in the entire monthly series.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_2451f00f854b4ca7a2523e20","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"python3 << 'EOF'\nimport re\n\nwith open('/app/resources/treasury_bulletin_1968_07_page_83.txt', 'r') as f:\n    content = f.read()\n\n# Let me extract the full data structure differently\n# Looking at the December row, I see years in the data\n# Let me find ALL rows with June and track which year corresponds to each value\n\n# Approach: \n# 1. Each row with a month has pattern: <td>Month</td>...\n# 2. Embedded in the row are year markers like <td>1962</td>\n# 3. The Treasury yield values appear in specific positions relative to these markers\n\n# Let me extract ALL June data with year markers properly\njune_data = []  # (year, treasury_yield)\n\nmonthly_section = content[content.find('Monthly series'):]\nrows = monthly_section.split('</tr><tr>')\n\n# Parse each row - I'll track position of each element\nfor row in rows:\n    if '<td>June</td>' in row:\n        # This is a June row\n        # Let's parse it cell by cell\n        \n        # Split into individual cell contents\n        cells = re.findall(r'<td([^>]*)>(.*?)</td>', row)\n        \n        # cells is list of (attributes, content) tuples\n        # We need to identify which are years and which are yields\n        \n        row_data = []\n        current_year = None\n        \n        for i, (attr, cell_content) in enumerate(cells):\n            cell_content = cell_content.strip()\n            # Check if this is a year (4-digit number)\n            if re.match(r'^\\d{4}$', cell_content):\n                current_year = int(cell_content)\n                row_data.append(('year', current_year))\n            # Check if this is a number (yield)\n            elif re.match(r'^[\\d.]+', cell_content):\n                # Extract the number (remove 2/ or 3/ footnote markers)\n                yield_val = re.sub(r'\\s*2/$', '', cell_content)\n                yield_val = re.sub(r'\\s*3/$', '', yield_val)\n                try:\n                    val = float(yield_val)\n                    row_data.append(('yield', val, current_year))\n                except:\n                    pass\n            elif cell_content in ['January', 'February', 'March', 'April', 'May', 'June', \n                                  'July', 'August', 'September', 'October', 'November', 'December']:\n                row_data.append(('month', cell_content))\n        \n        print(\"Parsed June row:\")\n        print(row_data)\n        print()\n\n# Now I need to figure out which yield belongs to which year\n# Looking at the pattern:\n# First few entries: month, yield (for first year), yield (moody), [year], yield, yield, [year], yield, yield\n# If no year is specified before a yield, it continues the sequence\n\n# Actually, I think the format is:\n# - First column pair is always for the section base year (e.g., 1957)\n# - Subsequent column pairs have explicit year markers\n\n# Let me map this by assuming first yield is for section year\nEOF"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
